=== why there was no lucky choice of line ===
each Fano line together with e0 is closed under multiplication and its three
units square to -1, i.e. it is a copy of H sitting inside O:
  (e0,e1,e2,e3): closed under multiplication = True, e^2 = -1 for all three = True
  (e0,e1,e4,e5): closed under multiplication = True, e^2 = -1 for all three = True
  (e0,e2,e4,e6): closed under multiplication = True, e^2 = -1 for all three = True
  (e0,e3,e4,e7): closed under multiplication = True, e^2 = -1 for all three = True
  (e0,e1,e7,e6): closed under multiplication = True, e^2 = -1 for all three = True
  (e0,e2,e5,e7): closed under multiplication = True, e^2 = -1 for all three = True
  (e0,e3,e6,e5): closed under multiplication = True, e^2 = -1 for all three = True
O has exactly 7 quaternion subalgebras containing 1, and they are exactly the
7 lines of the Fano plane.  A triad gate IS a quaternion subalgebra, so its
associator is zero by theorem, not by an accident of orientation.  There is no
orientation of the Fano plane, valid or otherwise, for which a triad gate reads
a non-zero associator.

the 28 triples that DO have a non-zero associator, in Table 1 variables:
  (e1,e2,e4) = (sigma_x, sigma_y, Q_top): |assoc| = 2.0
  (e1,e2,e5) = (sigma_x, sigma_y, helicity): |assoc| = 2.0
  (e1,e2,e6) = (sigma_x, sigma_y, valley): |assoc| = 2.0
  (e1,e2,e7) = (sigma_x, sigma_y, edge phase): |assoc| = 2.0
  ... 24 more, all of the same form.
every one of the 28 mixes a spin component with a skyrmion winding number, a
valley polarisation or an edge phase -- and closure.py shows that the product
of such states is never itself a physical state.  The two defects interlock:
the only gates whose observable is non-zero are the gates whose output the
hardware cannot hold.

