SOTP: 'immunity to parasitic magnetic fields up to 10 T' (Sec. 4.3)
========================================================================
  Ru RKKY coupling  0.5 mJ/m^2, Co 0.8 nm: spin-flop field   0.89 T
  Ru RKKY coupling  1.0 mJ/m^2, Co 0.8 nm: spin-flop field   1.79 T
  Ru RKKY coupling  2.0 mJ/m^2, Co 0.8 nm: spin-flop field   3.57 T
  Ru RKKY coupling  6.0 mJ/m^2, Co 0.8 nm: spin-flop field  10.71 T
  -> 10 T needs J_ex = 5.6 mJ/m^2, at the very top of the
     strongest Co/Ru coupling ever reported.  More to the point:
  stray fields inside a packaged chip are of order uT to mT, so a 10 T
  immunity figure is 4-7 orders above anything the device would meet.
  It is not a specification, it is decoration.

========================================================================
SOTP Sec. 6.1: octonions, SU(3) and the chiral condensate
========================================================================
  dim O = 8, of which 7 imaginary units; dim su(3) = 8 generators.
  these are different objects: Aut(O) = G2 (dim 14), and SU(3) appears as
  the subgroup of G2 fixing one imaginary unit.  The 8 coordinates of an
  octonion do not 'project onto the Gell-Mann matrices'; the matching
  count of 8 is a coincidence between an algebra dimension and a Lie
  algebra dimension.  Furey (ref. [3]) works with the left-adjoint action
  of the complexified octonions, not with the 8 coordinates.

  QCD scale Lambda_QCD                 : 2.000e+08 eV
  one 10 GHz spin-wave quantum         : 4.136e-05 eV = 41.36 ueV
  -> the excitation the SOTP can create is 4.84e+12 x too small to
     touch the chiral condensate or nucleon deconfinement.

